  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a spring gun having spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> a small ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is put in its barrel (as shown in figure) by compressing the spring through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. There should be a box placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> on the ground so that the ball falls in it. If the ball leaves the gun horizontally at a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> above the ground. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0071_07dff6cbb488.png\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 232px;\" /></p>"
  },
